e of a new member and parse JSON sidecars up front;\n(m) D27: role tokens can be COMPILER names (`gcc`/`tcc`) -- the generic longest-member-token peel handled them; the HCFG scan\nDIRECTION is in the question (\"scan backward from the end\") -- honour it per id; theme facts (producer, debug format, linker\nsection layout, libc) were unasked but are recorded in Recognition cues; (n) D28: look-alike members get MULTI-WORD role tokens\n(`family_a`, `false_friend`), unqualified ids are the consensus of the members the question NAMES with one EXCLUDED (it has its\nown valid config); a backfill can land on ANY day and spell every new field as a sentence -- implement the sentence, POST new\nfamilies alone, and treat ELF wording as also binding a PE re-roll (map to the PE twin field); (o) D29/D30: id tags can be\nSEMANTIC words absent from basenames (`optimized` -> `O3.elf`, `config_capsule` -> `config.n`): route on the question's \"basename\nends X\"; the config record's MAGIC can change (`HGRF`) with the layout kept -- decode any 4-byte magic the question names, and a\nJSON path's first segment may name the record (`graph.config.campaign` -> obj[\"config\"][\"campaign\"]); normalise as told\n(`this_role` omitted) before a consensus check; `none` is never right for a record you can decode.\nAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\nsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\nhcfg_resource_size, `<role>_machine` (D21 loader/plugin, integer), `<role>_format` + `<role>_config_*` (D24 vulnerable/corrected; D27 `<role>_machine` + `<role>_format` + `gcc_config_*`, roles gcc/tcc), `cras